Long-range constraints and contact supports

The C# joint graph, distance bounds, support footprints, active height solve
and load transfer adapt the project's research implementations from
codex/job331-380:

  tools/SomeEngine.Physics.Research/JointDistances.cs
  tools/SomeEngine.Physics.Research/Native/LongRange.cpp
  tools/SomeEngine.Physics.Research/Native/ContactSupports.cpp

The distance and contact support construction follows Long Range Constraints
for Rigid Body Simulations (SCA 2017), including the contact support polygon
and load propagation in section 3.6:
https://matthias-research.github.io/pages/publications/LongRangeConstraintsSCA.pdf

The current C# implementation retains auxiliary forces in joint/contact ECS
components, keeps local response work on body entities, and reuses the selected
Newton compliant ALM body's existing six-dimensional factorization.
